<Base title="Federal Tax Credits for Batteries & Heat Pumps Ended 12/31/2025: What's Left | HomeBackupCost" description="The 25D battery credit and 25C heat pump credit ended for work completed after 12/31/2025 under the One Big Beautiful Bill. Here's what the IRS says and what incentives remain." schema={[{ '@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity: faq.map(([q,a]) => ({ '@type':'Question', name:q, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:a } })) }]}>
<h1>The federal tax credits ended on 12/31/2025</h1>
<p class="lede">If you've seen "30% off your home battery with the federal tax credit," that offer is over for anything installed in 2026 or later.</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>25D: Residential Clean Energy Credit</h3><p>Was 30% for solar, <strong>battery storage</strong>, and geothermal.</p><p class="bad"><strong>Ended:</strong> installations completed after 12/31/2025 are not eligible.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>25C: Energy Efficient Home Improvement Credit</h3><p>Was 30%, up to $3,200 a year, for heat pumps, panels, and insulation.</p><p class="bad"><strong>Ended:</strong> property placed in service after 12/31/2025 is not eligible.</p></div>
</div>
<p class="src">Source: <a href={IRS}>IRS FAQs on the modification of sections 25C, 25D… under Public Law 119-21</a>. Checked 2026-10-25.</p>
<h2>What's still available</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>State HOMES/HEAR rebates</strong> funded by the Department of Energy, live in some states. <a href="/rebates/">Status by state →</a></li>
<li><strong>Utility rebates</strong>, mostly for heat pumps (for example DTE, Consumers Energy, ComEd, and Con Edison).</li>
<li><strong>California wildfire-area portable battery rebates</strong> from PG&amp;E, SDG&amp;E, and SCE. <a href="/rebates/ca/">CA page →</a></li>
</ul>
<p class="note">If your system was completed by 12/31/2025, you may still claim the credit on that tax year's return. Ask a tax professional; this is not tax advice.</p>
